    not_duplicate_of: []  # 21de
    pr_ref:  # 21de
    description: "## Context\n\nThe PlazaFlow team suggested four repos as a bakeoff curriculum targeting the three gaps identified for their codebase: CRDT reactive flow modeling, binary protocol dispatch, and abstraction-layer tracing. These repos should be cloned to ~/repos and used for DEEP-mode bakeoff analysis before building the Yjs linker and annotation convention.\n\n## Curriculum (ordered progression)\n\n### 1. yjs/yjs — Raw Yjs API surface catalog\n- **URL:** https://github.com/yjs/yjs\n- **Purpose:** Catalog the full Yjs API surface to define linker detection patterns\n- **What to study:** Y.Map, Y.Array, Y.Text, Y.Doc, observe, observeDeep, awareness.setLocalStateField, awareness.on('change'), transaction patterns\n- **Gap targeted:** CRDT reactive flow modeling (base case)\n- **Expected size:** Small (~2MB) — study cover-to-cover\n\n### 2. toeverything/blocksuite — Framework abstraction layer over Yjs\n- **URL:** https://github.com/toeverything/blocksuite\n- **Purpose:** Stress-test whether a Yjs linker can trace through BlockSuite's abstraction layer (slot-based events, computed properties from CRDT state, block schema system)\n- **What to study:** How block mutations and observations map to underlying Yjs operations; whether catching raw Yjs calls is sufficient or if BlockSuite-level patterns also need detection\n- **Gap targeted:** CRDT reactive flow modeling (layered abstractions)\n- **Expected size:** Large (~50-100MB)\n\n### 3. toeverything/AFFiNE — Real application consuming BlockSuite + Yjs\n- **URL:** https://github.com/toeverything/AFFiNE\n- **Purpose:** Validate whether hypergumbo's sketch and call graph produce useful output for a Yjs-heavy production application (same relationship PlazaFlow will have to BlockSuite)\n- **What to study:** Whether the call graph captures real data flow or just direct function calls; whether slice output is useful for understanding a feature\n- **Gap targeted:** End-to-end CRDT reactive flow validation\n- **Expected size:** Large (~100-200MB)\n\n### 4. versatica/mediasoup — Binary protocol dispatch + cross-language IPC\n- **URL:** https://github.com/versatica/mediasoup\n- **Purpose:** SFU with custom binary signaling protocol over WebRTC data channels — close to PlazaFlow's relay wire protocol. C++ worker + TypeScript/Node control layer.\n- **What to study:** Binary message type dispatch patterns; cross-language IPC between C++ worker and Node process; whether the annotation convention (@hg:publishes/@hg:subscribes) would be sufficient to capture dispatch semantics\n- **Gap targeted:** Binary protocol dispatch, cross-language boundary tracing\n- **Expected size:** Medium (~20-50MB)\n\n## Execution Plan\n\n1. Human clones repos to ~/repos\n2. Run DEEP-mode bakeoff: `./scripts/bakeoff-features init --pool ~/repos` then cohort with these four repos\n3. Analyze baseline hypergumbo output to understand what's captured vs missed\n4. Catalog Yjs API patterns from yjs/yjs source for linker implementation\n5. Record findings in lab notebook\n6. Use findings to inform implementation of the Yjs linker and annotation convention work items\n\n## Needs Human Review Because\n\n- Repos need to be manually cloned (network access for git clone)\n- Large repos (AFFiNE, BlockSuite) may need disk space consideration\n- Human should confirm these repos are appropriate bakeoff targets before committing time"  # 21de
    fields: {}  # 21de
